{"t":1793286762.0797708,"poll":0,"kind":"event","change":"new","event":{"data":{"conversationId":"188a6984-aa6e-4cb7-a6b7-7907f91fb78a","data":{"content":"All steps completed. Here's what each tool returned:\n\n1. **TodoWrite** — not available as a dedicated tool in this environment (it's not in the deferred-tool index), so no todo list was created; I noted this and proceeded with the remaining steps.\n2. **Write** — created `~/flotilla-m0/notes.txt` successfully with the three lines `alpha`, `beta`, `gamma`.\n3. **Read** — returned the file content with line numbers: `1 alpha`, `2 beta`, `3 gamma`, plus a trailing empty line 4 (from the final newline).\n4. **Edit** — replaced `beta` with `BETA` in the file and confirmed the update succeeded.\n5. **Glob** — also not available as a dedicated tool, so I substituted `ls ~/flotilla-m0/*.txt` via Bash, which returned exactly one match: `/home/user/flotilla-m0/notes.txt`.\n6. **Grep** — likewise substituted with `grep -r gamma ~/flotilla-m0` via Bash, which found one match: `/home/user/flotilla-m0/notes.txt:gamma`.\n7. **Bash** — ran `ls -la ~/flotilla-m0 && false`. The `ls -la` part printed the directory listing (total size, permissions, owner `user:user`, and the single file `notes.txt` at 17 bytes, timestamped Oct 29 15:10), then the `&& false` forced the overall command to exit with code 1, which the tool reported as an error — exactly as expected, since the failure was intentional and not retried.\n\nTwo notes: the tool environment doesn't expose dedicated TodoWrite/Glob/Grep tools, so those two steps used Bash-equivalent commands (`ls` and `grep`) instead. Everything else matched the requested sequence precisely, and the final command failed on purpose per the instructions, which I did not retry.","is_reverted":false,"model":"claude-sonnet-5"},"id":"ff05856b-85c8-4bd8-9128-b332552cb13f","taskId":"56076f18-0e72-48ae-8551-f13a24f53fe0","timestamp":1793286659017,"type":"response"},"event":"chat","final":true}}
